  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_squirrel_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>untanned skins of squirrels | the fur of one or other of various species of slender, graceful, agile rodents (characterized by a long bushy tail, furry coat, and bright eyes), belonging to the genus Sciurus, or to the widely-distributed sub-family Sciurina including this; especially the common species Sciurus vulgaris, native to Britain, Europe, and parts of Asia. (OED s.v. squirrel n.) | one or other of various species of slender, graceful, agile rodents (characterized by a long bushy tail, furry coat, and bright eyes), belonging to the genus Sciurus, or to the widely-distributed sub-family Sciurina including this; especially the common species Sciurus vulgaris, native to Britain, Europe, and parts of Asia. (OED s.v. squirrel n.)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
